ine/godot/pulls/115474","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115474","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115474.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115474.patch","merged_at":"2026-07-29T17:25:31Z"},"body":"Partially implements [this](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111936#discussion_r2456990964) suggestion of moving regex to core. Does not currently allow disabling `pcre2`/`regex` outright, which in practice adds ~0.3 MB to the minimal template (though that could likely be mitigated by not using built-ins). I attempted to keep the thirdparty logic as minimally invasive as possible in this migration, `regex.cpp` adds some defines directly and includes the built-in pcre2 header explicitly. It also simplifies the build process for the thirdparty files to only compile with 32-bits, as we were never using the 16-bit ones in practice (maybe ever, but certainly not since `String` used UTF-32 internally)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115474/reac